Build the AIR compute path as a shared library for the Metal driver.

tools/mesa/air/air_metal.c is air_run's compute path -- a Metal function's LLVM module
through the AIR frontend into a Gallium compute state and a grid on the GPU -- behind
the contract in tools/mesa/air/air_metal.h, which mentions nothing of NIR, Gallium or
the GPU's compiler: the Metal driver (userland/src/hakiosmetal_air.m) must not grow a
dependency on Mesa's headers for it. On the device it is /redwood/lib/libhakiosair.dylib,
which is where -newComputePipelineStateWithDescriptor: compiles the bitcode Metal hands
it (docs/metal.md 10.12). It opens the GPU the kernel serves: the Adreno through
freedreno (HakiosGPU) or the Galaxy S9's Mali through panfrost (HakiosMali).

Both targets are in a directory of their own, src/gallium/targets/hakiosair, read last:
they need libgallium and the GPU drivers, which meson has not defined when
src/compiler/air is read, and panfrost's directory is read after freedreno's, where they
were first declared.

air_metal_test is that library driven the way the driver will drive it, on softpipe: it
is handed the frontend's include directory and nothing else, so a call air_metal.h fails
to provide shows up as a test that cannot be written.

--- a/src/gallium/meson.build
+++ b/src/gallium/meson.build
@@ -272,3 +272,7 @@
   subdir('frontends/teflon')
   subdir('targets/teflon')
 endif
+
+# The Metal driver's compiler library (src/gallium/targets/hakiosair): last, because it takes
+# whichever GPU drivers were built above, freedreno's and panfrost's alike.
+subdir('targets/hakiosair')
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/gallium/targets/hakiosair/meson.build
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# libhakiosair: the same path air_run takes -- a Metal shader through the AIR frontend
+# into a compute state and a grid on the GPU -- as a shared library, for the Metal
+# driver in userland/src/hakiosmetal_air.m. Its contract is src/compiler/air/air_metal.h and
+# mentions nothing of Mesa; this is only where it is built: after every gallium driver,
+# because it takes whichever of the phones' GPU drivers the build has (freedreno for the
+# Adreno, panfrost for the Mali; each an empty dependency when it is not built), and meson
+# reads panfrost's directory after freedreno's, where this was first declared.
+hakiosair_link_args = []
+if host_machine.system() == 'darwin'
+  # the Metal driver links against this by name, so the name has to be where
+  # tools/mk-mesa.sh installs it on the device
+  hakiosair_link_args += '-Wl,-install_name,/redwood/lib/libhakiosair.dylib'
+endif
+
+libhakiosair = shared_library(
+  'hakiosair',
+  files('../../../compiler/air/air_metal.c'),
+  include_directories : [inc_include, inc_src, inc_mapi, inc_mesa, inc_gallium,
+                         inc_gallium_aux, inc_gallium_winsys_sw, inc_gallium_winsys,
+                         include_directories('../../drivers')],
+  dependencies : [dep_m, idep_air, idep_mesautil, driver_softpipe, driver_freedreno,
+                  driver_panfrost, dep_libdrm],
+  link_with : [libgallium, libgalliumvl_stub, libws_null],
+  link_args : hakiosair_link_args,
+  build_by_default : false,
+  install : false,
+)
+
+# air_metal_test: the library driven the way the driver will drive it, on softpipe. It is
+# given the frontend's include directory and nothing else, so that a call the contract
+# does not provide shows up as a test that cannot be written.
+air_metal_test = executable(
+  'air_metal_test',
+  files('../../../compiler/air/air_metal_test.c'),
+  include_directories : include_directories('../../../compiler/air'),
+  link_with : [libhakiosair],
+  build_by_default : false,
+  install : false,
+)
